<% content_for :title, "Scenarios" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag "scenarios", defer: true %>
<% end %>

<h1>Scenarios</h1>

<p class="lede">
  The traffic shapes the Reader exists to make readable, one button each. Every button below
  is also a <code>curl</code> line — see the example app README for the exact ones. This
  page's own requests are not excluded from capture.
</p>

<ul class="scenarios">
  <li>
    <button type="button" data-scenario="<%= scenario_parallel_path %>" data-count="4">
      1 — Parallel requests
    </button>
    <p class="meta">Four requests at once, each running a couple of queries, so their SQL interleaves.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <button type="button" data-scenario="<%= scenario_n_plus_one_path %>">
      2 — N+1
    </button>
    <p class="meta">One query for fifty comments, then one more per comment for its author.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <button type="button" data-scenario="<%= scenario_slow_query_path %>">
      3 — Slow query
    </button>
    <p class="meta">A recursive CTE, genuinely slow inside SQLite. No Ruby <code>sleep</code> involved.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <button type="button" data-scenario="<%= scenario_hang_path %>">
      4 — Hang
    </button>
    <p class="meta">Never finishes. Watch it climb in the Reader; reload this tab to give up on it.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <button type="button" data-scenario="<%= scenario_error_path %>">
      5 — 500 error
    </button>
    <p class="meta">An unhandled exception with a real backtrace.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <button type="button" data-scenario="<%= scenario_dual_homing_path %>">
      6 — Dual-homed log line
    </button>
    <p class="meta">A <code>Rails.logger</code> call sandwiched between two queries.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <button type="button" data-scenario="<%= scenario_raw_sql_path %>">
      7 — Raw SQL
    </button>
    <p class="meta">A bare <code>connection.execute</code>: no model, no binds, a <code>nil</code> name.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <button type="button" data-scenario="<%= scenario_flood_path %>" data-count="20">
      9 — Request flood
    </button>
    <p class="meta">The same cheap query, fired about twenty times at once.</p>
  </li>
</ul>

<p id="scenario-output" role="status"></p>
